							<table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody><tr><td class="ContentBoxBody"> <div align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><b>Cleric Epic</b></font><br /> </div> The Start</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Lake Rathetear - Hail Shmendrik Lavawalke (+3600, 0) to begin the quest. To save time, Kill this NPC now, and his spawn "Spirit of Flame". Loot the Damaged Goblin Crown. (this will save you time later, and possibly needing to do parts again.)</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Frozen Water 1</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Lake Rathetear - Find Lord Bergurgle (+2800, +150 in underwater cave at +2831, -912) . His placeholder is on a 28 minute timer. Kill Lord Bergurgle and loot Lord Bergurgle's Crown. **Note: Lord Bergurgle casts complete heal. Enduring breath is required. The ledge above the spawnpoint is very safe, and a good place to med. Begurgle is level 40, with about 6000hp.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Frozen Water 2</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Once you have Lord Begurgle's Crown, grab the Damaged Goblin Crown you looted in step 1, and go visit Schmedrik again. Give him Lord B's crown, and Natasha Whitewater will spawn. BE PATIENT HERE. Natasha is initially not visible to you as you do the hand-in - she spawns out of LOS. After 20-30 seconds or so, she will agro Shmedrik. You need not do anything except make sure that Shmedrik is rooted next to Natasha. Once Shmedrik does, the spirit of flame will spawn, and, if you did the first part right, will agro Natasha. If this doesn't happen, stand next to Natasha and nuke the spirit. Once Natasha is aggroed, she will kill the spirit of flame as well. Once the spirit is dead, give Natasha the Damaged Goblin Crown, and you will receive An Ornate Sea Shell, and her thanks. Important note: do not skip step 1 - you must have the Damaged Crown to do it this way!! If Natasha gets the killing blow on the spirit of flame, the corpse will poof, and you will have no Damaged Goblin Crown to give to Natasha! This means you'd have to camp Begurgle again.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Frozen Water 3</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Tim. Deep - Omar Vastsea, This fine fellow is at loc (neg 11567, neg 2227). To reach him, take the cave entrance at loc ( neg 11530, neg 3728), then the entrance at (neg 11336, neg 1307). Give him the Ornate Sea Shell, and he will give you A Coral Statue of Tarew.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Frozen Water 4</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">AKA Long Boring Camp II. Gimblox is in Solusek's Eye (SolA), at exactly loc neg796, neg366. This is in the room adjacent to the King Room. Gimblox and his placeholder (a large fire goblin) are on a nineteen minute timer. There are two other static spawns in the room, plus a wanderer. All of these are easily handled by anyone seriously contemplating an epic. Gimblox himself is level 30, with about 1800 hp -- the placeholders and other spawns are weaker. This is an excellent opportunity for powerleveling, as you can keep this room, the king room, and the mage/priest spawn near there cleared fairly easily. Gimblox drops Lord Gimblox's Signet Ring</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Frozen Water 5</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">You will need at least one group of 50+ to succeed here. The priest can be found in the Temple of Solusek Ro, at loc (pos 326, pos 38, pos 29). This is up on the second floor. The priest is level 55, about 3500 hit points, and summons. He likes to nuke and heal, and is unstunnable. He spawns at 9am and despawns at 9pm each game day. The easiest way to kill the priest is to have a tank pull the priest to the zoneline and either FD (if monk) or zone. The rest of the party is waiting in the hallway, including the cleric. The cleric gives the priest the Coral Statue of Tarew, and the priest then agros the rest of the party. Loot the Blood-Soaked Plasmatic Priest Robe.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Frozen Water 6</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Timorous Deep - Go see Omar again. Give him the blood-soaked robe from the Plasmatic Priest, and you get the Orb of Frozen Water, and Natasha Whitewater spawns (inside the inn -- go in and turn left). Give Gimblox's Ring to Natasha, and you get an Ornate Sea Shell.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Clean Water</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">NOTE: This, and all subsequent encounters, require at least three balanced groups of 50+ adventurers. The more, the better. Overkill is a good thing here. Find Naxot Deepwater in Burning Woods, approx. loc (pos 3400, neg 2150). Give her the Ornate Sea Shell, and you'll get a Message to Natasha, and Ixiblat Fer will spawn. Ixi is a fire elemental lord, level 62, about 32000hp, with a resistible 300hp DD AOE fire attack. The most common practice is to have a bard or ranger pull Ixi to the Skyfire zoneline, an open area free from adds. He can and should be slowed, and will run when low on health. Loot the Sceptre of Ixiblat Fer from his corpse.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Clean Water 2</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">This encounter also requires at least three groups of 50+ adventurers. The Overking is one of the Royals in Chardok, get a map for his exact spawn point. The Overking is at least level 63, and has an AOE Fiery Death (approx 500 hp dmg, cancels 1 buff). He also likes to complete heal, and cast Gravity Flux and Gate. He spawns every two hours. Loot the Singed Scroll from his corpse.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Clean Water 3</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Tim Deep - Go see Omar again, and give him the sceptre and scroll. He will give you the Orb of Clear Water, and Natasha will spawn again. Give Natasha the Message to Natasha you got from Naxot, and Natasha will give you a Shimmering Pearl.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Vapor 1</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Go to Nagafen's Lair (SolB), to approximately neg 1300, neg 300. Look for a banner there, Zordak will spawn there. Zordak will only spawn once every 24 hours. Give him the Shimmering Pearl, and you'll get a Swirling Pearl, plus a Box of Binding. The Box of Binding is a container, be sure you have room for it.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Vapor 2</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Now go to Skyfire and collect four Pearlescent Fragments. Apparently they can and do drop rarely off nearly every mob in the zone. Once you have four, put them in the Box of Binding and hit combine. You will now have an Assembled Pearlescent Shard.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of Vapor 3</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Find Warder Cecilia in Skyfire, at pos 3200 neg 3200, in front of the big dragon statue. Give Cecilia the Assembled Pearlescent Shard, and the human form of Ragefire will spawn. The human form is level 55. When the human form of Zordak is killed, Zordakalicus Ragefire (the dragon form) will spawn. The dragon is level 60, and is similar in strength to Lord Nagafen. When the dragon form is killed, loot the Impure Heart of Ragefire.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of the Vapor</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Tim Deep - Place the swirling pearl and the Pearlescent Seal (that you got from Cecilia when you turned in the shard) inside the impure heart, and hit combine. The container becomes "Heart of Ragefire". Take the Heart back to Omar Vastsea, and he will give you the Orb of Vapor, and Jhassad Oceanson will spawn.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Orb of the Triumvirate 1</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Tim Deep - Give Jhassad the three orbs, and he will return the Orb of the Triumvirate, and the Avatar of Water will spawn.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody><tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">The "Click- Stick"</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Give the Avatar the Orb of the Triumvirate, and you will receive the Water Sprinkler of Nem Ankh.</td></tr></tbody> </table> 
							
